# Cursor Rules for InvestTech UI Components

## Component Library Guidelines

### Use shadcn/ui Components Only
- **Only use components from shadcn/ui** - This is a strict requirement for all UI components
- When implementing new components, base them on shadcn/ui patterns and components
- Do not create custom component implementations when a shadcn/ui equivalent exists
- Always prefer shadcn/ui components over custom implementations

### shadcn/ui Installation & Usage
- Use `npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>` to add components
- Components should be installed individually as needed
- Follow shadcn/ui's theming and customization patterns
- Maintain consistency with shadcn/ui design tokens and variants

### Component Development
- All components must follow shadcn/ui's component API patterns
- Use the same prop interfaces and naming conventions as shadcn/ui
- Implement proper TypeScript types matching shadcn/ui standards
- Follow accessibility patterns established by shadcn/ui

### Styling & Theming
- Use Tailwind CSS classes as defined by shadcn/ui components
- Maintain the existing design token system alongside shadcn/ui
- Ensure components are themeable and support light/dark modes
- Follow shadcn/ui's CSS variable approach for theming

### Code Quality
- Components must be fully typed with TypeScript
- Follow React best practices and hooks patterns
- Ensure proper component composition and reusability
- Write clean, maintainable code following shadcn/ui conventions

### When to Create Custom Components
- Only when no suitable shadcn/ui component exists
- Custom components must still follow shadcn/ui design patterns
- Consider contributing back to shadcn/ui if creating broadly useful components
- Document any custom components thoroughly

### Imports & Dependencies
- Import components from the local shadcn/ui setup
- Avoid importing external component libraries unless absolutely necessary
- Keep dependencies minimal and focused on shadcn/ui ecosystem
- Use custom-styling 